<div style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 15px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # Introducing Panama to the World – Lesson # 5</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0; font-size: 1.1em;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 5</p></td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Mediation</p></td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Grade:</b> 12th Grade (CEFR: B1.3)</p></td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Scenario:</b> International Communication</p></td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Theme:</b> Introducing Panama to the World</p></td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</p></td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; colspan="2""><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</p></td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; colspan="3"">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Mediation: Concept: Explain complex ideas with simple examples. Concept: Clarify abstract concepts, using practical illustrations.</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; colspan="3"">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Mediation: Can explain Panama's global importance using simple visuals like maps and charts (e.g., uses a map to show how the Panama Canal reduces shipping routes between Asia and Europe by thousands of miles). Can clarify abstract concepts on international trade with practical illustrations (e.g., illustrates "trade routes" by drawing arrows on a map). Can use body language and bilingual keywords to aid in comprehension (e.g., gestures to indicate trade flow and explains terms in both English and Spanish).</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; color: #1a5276; width: 35%;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; color: #1a5276; width: 50%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; color: #1a5276; width: 15%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</b><br>(Engagement, Modeling and Clarification)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher displays a large world map and points to Panama. Students are asked: "What makes Panama a strategic location on this map?" and "Why is the Panama Canal considered a global trade hub?" (Stress Wh- question words). Students share initial ideas, activating vocabulary like 'trade', 'global', 'hub', 'strategic', 'impact', 'routes'.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher models how to explain "global trade hub" simply. "A global trade hub is like a central meeting point, or a crossroads, for products and services from all over the world. It’s where many different shipping routes intersect, making it easier and faster for companies to move goods. Panama is recognized for its trade influence because of its central location." The teacher gestures to indicate flow and connection.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"If I explain a complex idea, why should I use simple examples?" (To make it easier for others to understand.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Can a map or a drawing help clarify an abstract concept like 'trade routes'?" (Yes, it provides a visual illustration.)</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5-7 min</p></td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 2 — Presentation</b><br>(Input of new language/content)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A short documentary excerpt (3-4 minutes) or an infographic about the economic impact of the Panama Canal on global shipping and trade, focusing on key statistics and benefits. The content will include information about financial services, multinational companies, and the reduction of shipping routes.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Lead presentations on Panama's global role, ensuring all viewpoints are acknowledged and effectively communicated.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b> Students watch/read and answer gist questions related to the core message:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is the main idea presented about Panama's relevance in international commerce?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"According to the material, how does the Canal impact global shipping routes and time?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Which sectors in Panama are recognized for attracting multinational companies?"</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">7-10 min</p></td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</b><br>(Accuracy focus)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Students practice explaining and clarifying using Passive voice (e.g., "Panama is recognized for..."), Modals of necessity (e.g., "Students must be proficient..."), and Relative clauses (e.g., "a trade hub that connects..."). Vocabulary: 'trade', 'relevance', 'hub', 'impact', 'strategic', 'financial services', 'shipping', 'routes', 'commerce', 'global'. Pronunciation: /t/ in "trade", /g/ in "global", stressing modal verbs (MUST).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Activity 1 (Controlled Practice - Sentence Simplification):</b> Students are given complex sentences from the input material (e.g., "The interoceanic waterway, which significantly reduces transit times for international shipping, is operated by the Panama Canal Authority."). In pairs, they rewrite these sentences using simpler vocabulary and passive voice, aiming to explain the core idea to a non-expert. E.g., "Panama's canal is operated to reduce shipping times." They must include at least one relative clause.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Activity 2 (Semi-controlled - Explaining a Concept):</b> The teacher provides abstract concepts related to Panama's economy (e.g., "logistics hub," "biodiversity conservation," "financial sector"). Students choose one and prepare a 1-minute explanation for a partner, focusing on using simple examples, practical illustrations (e.g., drawing arrows on a mini-map for 'logistics hub'), and incorporating modals of necessity (e.g., "You MUST understand that the Canal's efficiency is critical."). They are encouraged to use body language and bilingual keywords if needed to aid comprehension.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Activity 3 (Pair Interaction - Peer Mediation Check):</b> Students take turns explaining their chosen concept from Activity 2 to their partner. The listener assesses how well the explanation clarified the concept, if visuals were helpful, and if the language was simple enough. They use prompts like: "From my perspective, your explanation was clear because you used X example," or "Could you clarify 'financial services' a bit more simply?"</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">15-20 min</p></td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</b><br>(Communicative task)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative task:</b> Students work in groups (of 3-4) to plan and present a 3-minute segment of their "Panama Introduction Video." Each group focuses on a specific aspect of Panama's global importance (e.g., Canal's economic impact, biodiversity relevance, cultural diversity, financial services sector). Their presentation must demonstrate strong mediation skills: explaining complex ideas with simple examples, clarifying abstract concepts with practical illustrations (e.g., showing a simplified map or chart), and using appropriate language (passive voice, relative clauses, modals) for an international audience. They MUST be proficient in English to successfully engage internationally.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task format:</b> Small group presentation of a planned video segment, using visual aids (sketches, simplified charts, maps) as if they were part of their video. They will verbally explain their segment to the class.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Focus:</b> Fluency in explaining, clarity of mediated information, effective use of simple visuals and practical illustrations, collaborative interaction, and comprehensive use of target grammar and vocabulary. Groups must ensure all viewpoints on their topic are acknowledged and communicated effectively.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10-12 min</p></td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</b><br>(Formative assessment)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative assessment strategy:</b> Teacher observation using a rubric focused on mediation skills and peer feedback. Each group will receive constructive feedback from their classmates.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Each group presents their planned 3-minute video segment. They will explain a key aspect of Panama's global role, ensuring they simplify complex terms and illustrate abstract concepts. The use of simple maps, charts, or diagrams to explain things like "trade routes" or "shipping impact" is critical. They should also demonstrate good pronunciation of /t/ and /g/ sounds and stress modal verbs.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Clarity and simplicity of explanations for complex ideas (Mediation).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Effective use of practical illustrations/visuals (maps, charts) to clarify concepts.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Accurate and appropriate use of passive voice, relative clauses, and modals of necessity.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Intelligible pronunciation, specifically for /t/ in "trade" and /g/ in "global", and stressing modals (e.g., "MUST").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Relevant use of target vocabulary (e.g., 'global', 'trade', 'hub', 'impact', 'strategic').</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Ability to engage the audience and acknowledge different viewpoints.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How effectively did my group explain a complex idea about Panama's global importance using simple examples today?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What specific visual aid or body language did I use to help my audience understand, and how effective was it?"</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">8-10 min</p></td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 6 — Reflection</b></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was the most challenging part of simplifying information about Panama for a global audience, and what strategy did I find most useful?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How can I apply these mediation skills to other academic subjects or future professional interactions where I need to explain complex concepts?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b> What worked well during the mediation tasks? Were students able to effectively simplify complex ideas and use visuals? Were the grammatical structures (passive voice, relative clauses, modals) integrated naturally into their explanations? What adjustments are needed to further scaffold students' ability to clarify abstract concepts and use body language or bilingual keywords effectively for improved comprehension in future mediation tasks?</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson in the theme sequence:</b> This lesson concludes the "Introducing Panama to the World" theme. The mediation skills practiced will be crucial for the upcoming unit on "Global Challenges and Solutions," where students will need to explain complex problems and proposed solutions to a diverse audience, continuing to apply these essential communication strategies.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5 min</p></td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>